---
description: CyberTalks agent rules — read the private coordination handoff and log first; PR wording GO then merge; separate deploy GO; public-text hygiene
alwaysApply: true
---

1. Before exploring or editing, read the private coordination repo's `AGENT_HANDOFF.md` and recent `AGENT_LOG.md`. Claim your task there and update both when you start, finish, or pause. If you cannot see that repo, stop and ask the maintainer.
2. Pull requests: draft the exact title and body in chat and wait for the maintainer's wording GO; after the GO, open and merge right away. No PR comments without the same GO. Delete merged branches.
3. A production deploy needs its own named GO. Do not start preview or production builds unless the maintainer names that action.
4. Everything in this repo is public. Never copy coordination files or private notes here, and never use internal project, pipeline, or vendor nicknames in code, comments, docs, data, or commit messages. Check the diff before pushing.
5. No GitHub link or star button on the site.
6. Inside Cursor, use Cursor-native models only unless the maintainer approves another model for that run.
